From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:12:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: re-select UTMI as pipe clk on resume

On msm8998 (Google Pixel 2 XL) the USB gadget does not survive s2idle.
After resume the UDC still reports state=configured / current_speed=
high-speed while the host sees no bus activity at all -- no connect, no
disconnect, not even a failed enumeration, across a physical unplug and
replug. Only a reboot restores it. A configfs unbind and rebind does
not, and prints:

    dwc3 a800000.usb: failed to enable ep0out

ep0 is the control endpoint, so enumeration is impossible.

The cause is one register. QSCRATCH_GENERAL_CFG reads 0x0000000d on a
fresh boot -- PIPE_UTMI_CLK_SEL and PIPE3_PHYSTATUS_SW set by
dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk() at probe -- and 0x00000004 after a resume,
with both bits gone. QSCRATCH sits in the USB GDSC, which collapses over
suspend, and nothing re-applies the selection. This board has no SSPHY
in use (maximum-speed = high-speed), so the pipe clock is the UTMI
clock: without that selection the core has no pipe clock, the DEPCFG
that enables ep0out cannot complete, and dwc3_core_init() during resume
programs a controller whose clock is not running.

Re-apply it in dwc3_qcom_resume(). Ordering works out for free: the glue
resumes before the core re-initialises, so the core sees a valid pipe
clock by the time dwc3_core_init_for_resume() runs.

Confirmed the mechanism from userspace before writing this: after a
resume, poking GENERAL_CFG back to 0x0000000d makes the ep0out failure
stop -- a gadget rebind then completes with no error -- but the bus
stays dead, because by then the core has already been initialised
without its clock. The bits have to be right before the core resumes,
which is exactly what this hook does.

Not board-specific: any platform with qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk and a
collapsing USB GDSC loses the same bits.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ded2ca86670c..230cb84e9c3f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ struct dwc3_qcom {
 	enum usb_dr_mode	mode;
 	bool			is_suspended;
 	bool			pm_suspended;
+	bool			ignore_pipe_clk;
 	struct icc_path		*icc_path_ddr;
 	struct icc_path		*icc_path_apps;
 
@@ -89,6 +90,8 @@ struct dwc3_qcom {
 
 #define to_dwc3_qcom(d) container_of((d), struct dwc3_qcom, dwc)
 
+static void dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom);
+
 static inline void dwc3_qcom_setbits(void __iomem *base, u32 offset, u32 val)
 {
 	u32 reg;
@@ -388,6 +391,15 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_resume(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(qcom->dev, "failed to enable interconnect: %d\n", ret);
 
+	/*
+	 * QSCRATCH sits in the USB GDSC, which collapses while we are
+	 * suspended, so the probe-time pipe-clk selection does not survive.
+	 * Re-apply it here: this glue resumes before the core re-initialises,
+	 * so the core has a valid pipe clock by then.
+	 */
+	if (qcom->ignore_pipe_clk)
+		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
+
 	/* Clear existing events from PHY related to L2 in/out */
 	for (i = 0; i < qcom->num_ports; i++) {
 		dwc3_qcom_setbits(qcom->qscratch_base,
@@ -615,7 +627,6 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct resource		res;
 	struct resource		*r;
 	int			ret;
-	bool			ignore_pipe_clk;
 	bool			wakeup_source;
 
 	qcom = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*qcom), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -678,9 +689,9 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * Disable pipe_clk requirement if specified. Used when dwc3
 	 * operates without SSPHY and only HS/FS/LS modes are supported.
 	 */
-	ignore_pipe_clk = device_property_read_bool(dev,
-				"qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk");
-	if (ignore_pipe_clk)
+	qcom->ignore_pipe_clk =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk");
+	if (qcom->ignore_pipe_clk)
 		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
 
 	qcom->mode = usb_get_dr_mode(dev);
